Hello and welcome to my x16 repo This branch is dedicated to the cpu V3x16 is a 16bit cpu whic uses a custom instruction set i developed It is palned to be only have 14 arithemetic instructions and 7 conditional instructions, The instructions are info are in the InstructionSet file
the prog.hex is a test program used by the testbench it contains a program that multiples 7 by 3

for current output testing i have a working general purpose output port like gpio but only output it is conected to r2

The cpu.v has the main module that are packed into functional cpu and require a rom to run as i dont know how to write a hardware rom in verilog. the main CPU module i in cpu/cpu.v and the testbench is in cpu/testbench.v
The assembler is a python script It is in assembler/X16A to use it you type [Path of the script] [input file] [output file] The assmebler alos produces a .hex file that the test bench can use Curently the rom module in testbench.v is limited but you can increase it as i dot know much about testbench syntax yet.
